@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk declares "SEE LICENSE IN README.md" and ships
a proprietary Anthropic licence (all rights reserved, Commercial Terms, no
OSI grant). It must not be compiled into the executable. Nothing imports
the SDK's values statically: every source import outside the single
`export *` in claude/agent-sdk.ts is `import type` (erased at build time),
and agent-sdk.ts is reached only through the dynamic import("#claude-agent-sdk")
in claude/sdk.ts load(), whose .catch degrades to the designed "Claude Agent
SDK isn't installed" error. Marking the package external leaves that dynamic
import unresolved at bundle time, so the provider fails soft at runtime
instead of shipping proprietary code. The SDK is already an optional
peerDependency of @opencode/core for exactly this shape.

--- a/packages/cli/script/build.ts
+++ b/packages/cli/script/build.ts
@@ -169,7 +169,7 @@
       simulationGraphPlugin,
       modelsSnapshot,
     ],
-    external: ["node-gyp"],
+    external: ["node-gyp", "@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk"],
     format: "esm",
     minify: true,
     bytecode: true,
